<title>USA: HIGH PLAINS WHEAT - ISOLATED PROTECTION REPORTED.</title>
<headline>HIGH PLAINS WHEAT - ISOLATED PROTECTION REPORTED.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly steady on Thursday amid isolated reports of two cents a bushel protection in Kansas, dealers said.</p>
<p>They noted conditions were nervous amid some uncertainty as to why the futures market rose so sharply on Wednesday and concern that it may fall back Thursday.</p>
<p>There were some calls for a higher futures opening following news that the European Union had raised its export tax and that U.S. weekly export sales were stronger than expected. Movement was generally slow.  </p>
